class_name MmoClasses
extends RefCounted
## The raid's six classes after WoW Classic: their looks (Black | White's
## armour, clothes, hair and weapons), stats, resource and eight abilities
## each on 1-8 (G39), one per slot of the author's template (`kind`):
##   1 spam          instant, ~3 s cooldown, beats auto-attacking
##   2 strong        instant, 10-12 s cooldown
##   3 self_steroid  1 s cast, 30 s; recast off cooldown to keep your damage up
##   4 team_steroid  instant, 30 s; recast off cooldown to keep the raid's up
##   5 self_heal     20 s cooldown
##   6 self_cleanse  30 s cooldown (every burn and curse on you)
##   7 super         1 s cast, big damage (the priest: a big group heal), 40 s
##   8 pick          the class's own: Taunt, Flash of Light, Dispel, Blink,
##                   Disengage, Sprint
## The sixteen-ability kits from G22 wait on each class's `shelf`, unused.
##
## An ability is data; MmoSim runs its `fx` list:
##   dmg n            damage to the target (crit 10%)          school = ab.school
##   aoe n, r, at     damage to enemies within r of "self" / "target"
##   dot n, dur       damage over time on the target (one aura per ability)
##   heal n           heal the target (an ally; yourself if none)
##   hot n, dur       heal over time
##   group_heal n, r  heal every living ally within r of you
##   shield n, dur    absorb
##   buff {mods}, dur, who   self / target / raid; mods: dmg haste dr speed crit threat regen maxhp heal
##   debuff {mods}, dur      on the enemy target: taken (damage taken x), swing (its swing time x), dmg (its damage x)
##   immune dur       nothing hurts; casting is blocked while it lasts when `still` is set
##   taunt            the boss turns on you
##   drop_threat f    lose this share of your threat
##   dash d, dir      "target" (to it), "behind" (behind it), "forward", "back"
##   res f            bring a dead ally back at this share of HP
##   gain n           resource
##   cp n             combo points (rogue); `finisher` consumes them and scales per_cp
##   cleanse          remove one cleansable debuff from an ally
##   mana f           restore this share of max mana
##   full_heal        to full HP
##   instant_next     the next cast-time spell is instant
##   crit_next        the next ability crits
##   ground ticks, every, r   a ground area at the target (Blizzard, Volley, Consecration)
## Rules on an ability: cd, cast, channel (s), ticks (channel), cost, gcd,
## range (0 = self / no target), tgt (enemy / ally / self / none / dead),
## behind (must be behind the target), exec (target under 20%), threat (x).
## `ai` tells the bots when to press it.

